conjgrad; training of a multilayer perceptron network and evaluation
of exact Hessian.

W. Penny, Imperial College, March 3 1998

-------------------------------------------------------------

Type 'make' to create the executable 'conjgrad'.

Edit the file conjgrad.c, and create new cost functions and
derivatives of cost functions, which are called from 
the frpmn routine in the optimise function.

Currently the cost function used is 'reg_xent' or 'reg_mse', which is the
cost of a single hidden layer mlp with sigmoid or linear output nodes trained
on a regularised cross entropy/mean squared error cost.

To test the compiled routine type:

conjgrad

This tells you what parameters are required. Now try:

conjgrad example/sinewave example/in_weights example/hypers 1 4 1 regress conjgrad 0.001 100 example/out_weights example/out_hessian


The currently compiled version is for Solaris 2.5.1



